  "result": "I haven't found anything that looks broken, so I don't have a fix to plan yet.\n\nThis repo is the Click library itself, not an app with its own CLI. It has no console script, so there is no single `--help` output to look at. Click builds help for whatever commands someone writes with it. The code in `src/click/core.py` and `decorators.py` matches Click's normal behaviour:\n\n- **Order:** options appear in the order they are declared in the source, with the auto-added `--help` last.\n- **Sorting:** nothing sorts options. Only the subcommand list in a group is alphabetical.\n- **Arguments:** these go in their own \"Positional arguments\" section.\n\nI can't tell which of these you mean by \"weird order\", so a few questions:\n\n1. Which command's `--help` did you see? An example command, or one you wrote with Click? A snippet of the output would help.\n2. What order did you expect? For example, alphabetical, required options first, or `--help` first.\n3. Should the change apply to every Click command, or only to one command? A library-wide change, such as a new sort option or a different default order, would break the many tests that assert on help output.\n\nOnce you answer, I'll write up the plan. Note that I couldn't use the question tool in this session, so I'm asking here instead.",
